The chance of getting one wish from one #sit is 1/39 [assuming 
sufficient luck]. The chance of not getting a wish, but the throne 
remaining, is (38/39)*(2/3)=76/117. So the chance of getting a first 
wish on the second #sit is (76/117)*(1/39), and so on. This gives a 
geometric series, which sums to (1/39)/(1 - 76/117)=3/41. So this is the 
chance of getting at least one wish from a throne.

There is a 2/3 chance the throne stays after the first wish, so there is 
a (2/3)*(1/39)=2/117 chance of a second wish on the next #sit, or a 
(2/3)*(3/41)=2/41 chance of getting a second wish at all. (The same is 
true for all subsequent wishes.)

So it's either a 2/1599 chance of getting two consecutive wishes, or 
6/1681 chance of getting two wishes from the same throne.


